{
  "title": "Numbers and counting",
  "note": "Only unus, duo and tres change form to match their noun (unus, una, unum; duo, duae, duo; tres, tria); quattuor to centum never change. Roman numerals: I 1, V 5, X 10, L 50, C 100, D 500, M 1000; a smaller numeral before a larger one subtracts: IV is 4, XC is 90.",
